  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41123-PROJECT-180098</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41123" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Industrial Development Organization</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the capacity of China&apos;s food inspection and testing bodies to improve trust for trade along the Belt and Road</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With the view to strengthening partnership between UNIDO and China to jointly promote Inclusive and Sustainable Industrial Development (ISID) within the framework of the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development of the United Nations, UNIDO signed with the former AQSIQ, the leading ministry for quality infrastructure development a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on 14 May 2017 during the Belt and Road Forum for International Cooperation in Beijing. The two sides agreed to develop collaboratively specific joint activities, projects and programmes in this regard. To this end, discussions and consultations with AQSIQ and its succeeding ministry, the State Administration for Market Regulation (SAMR) have been conducted on various occasions since 2017. In January 2018, the Deputy Chief Administrator of China Certification and Accreditation Administration (CNCA), Ms. DONG Lequn visited UNIDO Country Office in Beijing and requested UNIDO to support establishing a joint QI training centre. At the meeting on 6 November 2018 during the first China International Import Expo, Ms. Dong, as the DDG of the Department of Accreditation, Inspection and Testing of SAMR, further requested for UNIDO supports in capacity building to testing and inspection bodies in China aimed at facilitating trade flows between China and countries</narrative>
  </description>
